1
00:00:17,713 --> 00:00:20,170
I can't thank you enough, honestly.

2
00:00:20,253 --> 00:00:21,330
I should thank you.

3
00:00:21,413 --> 00:00:24,825
I appreciate you always calling
on me to help, Antistella.

4
00:00:27,173 --> 00:00:29,933
I'll see you again soon, Noor.

5
00:00:46,993 --> 00:00:48,593
Nice work today, Noor.

6
00:00:49,133 --> 00:00:53,662
And thanks to you, we'll have no problem
sticking to the schedule this month.

7
00:00:53,893 --> 00:00:55,253
Yeah, glad to hear it!

8
00:00:58,033 --> 00:00:58,913
What's that?

9
00:01:00,593 --> 00:01:02,073
Someone! Please help me!

10
00:01:04,253 --> 00:01:05,413
Hey! No!

11
00:01:17,453 --> 00:01:18,733
That's... huge!

12
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:26,210
Now I'm going to fly.

13
00:01:26,293 --> 00:01:29,190
I'm going to fly.

14
00:01:29,273 --> 00:01:30,593
I'm going to fly.

15
00:01:36,933 --> 00:01:43,710
When I'm on a cloud, I'll fly.

16
00:01:43,793 --> 00:01:44,623
I'll fly.

17
00:01:44,706 --> 00:01:45,536
I'll fly.

18
00:01:45,619 --> 00:01:46,933
I'll fly. There's nothing to say.?

19
00:01:48,313 --> 00:01:52,273
What do you want?

20
00:02:21,973 --> 00:02:22,803
Thank you so much for watching.

21
00:03:20,053 --> 00:03:21,773
Here, drink up.

22
00:03:22,673 --> 00:03:23,930
But be careful, Mom.

23
00:03:24,013 --> 00:03:25,453
It might be too hot.

24
00:03:26,693 --> 00:03:28,793
It's perfect. Thank you, son.

25
00:03:31,153 --> 00:03:32,490
Time to feed the goats.

26
00:03:32,573 --> 00:03:34,790
I'll take them to the
pasture over by the hill.

27
00:03:34,873 --> 00:03:36,410
Noor, now please be careful.

28
00:03:36,493 --> 00:03:37,323
I know, Mom.

29
00:03:37,453 --> 00:03:39,610
I won't go any further than the big rock.

30
00:03:39,693 --> 00:03:40,523
I promise.

31
00:03:40,893 --> 00:03:43,610
I'll get a wild rabbit and
some nuts and seeds later.

32
00:03:43,693 --> 00:03:44,634
We'll have soup.

33
00:03:49,733 --> 00:03:50,573
Hold on.

34
00:03:50,773 --> 00:03:52,538
I'll boil you some more water.

35
00:03:52,733 --> 00:03:53,563
Noor!

36
00:03:55,093 --> 00:03:55,993
What's wrong?

37
00:04:05,453 --> 00:04:08,113
I'm so sorry I can't do anything for you.

38
00:04:08,573 --> 00:04:12,173
But please, Noor, live the
life you wish to leave.

39
00:04:23,953 --> 00:04:25,613
Soup's ready!

40
00:04:29,633 --> 00:04:30,463
Mother?

41
00:04:35,573 --> 00:04:36,403
Mom?

42
00:04:38,473 --> 00:04:39,303
Mom!

43
00:04:51,553 --> 00:04:53,113
Let's go.

44
00:05:36,293 --> 00:05:39,253
Oh, my God.

45
00:05:46,473 --> 00:05:48,013
Nor, it's time for bed.

46
00:05:48,693 --> 00:05:50,073
What's tonight's story?

47
00:05:50,533 --> 00:05:52,153
It's about an adventurer.

48
00:05:52,493 --> 00:05:53,833
What's an adventurer?

49
00:05:54,213 --> 00:05:58,293
Well, son, this one, with
the help of his friends,

50
00:05:58,473 --> 00:06:02,673
slayed a gigantic dragon and learned
magic spells from an old sorcerer,

51
00:06:02,813 --> 00:06:04,613
broke a curse upon a forest,

52
00:06:04,813 --> 00:06:08,553
and even got a magic elixir
from the king of the dead.

53
00:06:09,493 --> 00:06:10,905
No matter the situation,

54
00:06:11,153 --> 00:06:15,690
an adventurer will raise their sword and
strike down evil for those who cannot.

55
00:06:15,773 --> 00:06:17,538
Shall I start reading it then?

56
00:06:17,993 --> 00:06:19,287
Yes, read it, read it!

57
00:06:19,433 --> 00:06:22,433
Alright, now settle in and
get ready for adventure.

58
00:06:24,193 --> 00:06:25,313
An adventurer?

59
00:06:26,533 --> 00:06:30,053
But please, Norm, live
the life you wish to lead.

60
00:06:38,553 --> 00:06:40,377
Don't eat it all at once, okay?

61
00:06:45,053 --> 00:06:48,113
Dad, Mom, I'm going.

62
00:06:48,453 --> 00:06:50,850
I'm leaving town for the first time ever.

63
00:06:50,933 --> 00:06:53,373
To become an adventurer!

64
00:06:56,433 --> 00:06:57,813
I'll make you proud.

65
00:07:29,273 --> 00:07:30,673
Oh

66
00:07:49,713 --> 00:07:52,073
Just off the main road. Thank you, sir.

67
00:08:22,813 --> 00:08:23,793
This is it!

68
00:08:29,373 --> 00:08:32,138
This place isn't for kids
to be hanging around.

69
00:08:32,293 --> 00:08:33,469
Now get out of here.

70
00:08:34,593 --> 00:08:39,122
The guards at the gate said I could be
an adventurer if I came to this place.

71
00:08:39,253 --> 00:08:40,190
Don't be an idiot!

72
00:08:40,273 --> 00:08:42,490
Your parents are probably worried sick.

73
00:08:42,573 --> 00:08:43,453
They're dead.

74
00:08:43,993 --> 00:08:44,913
Both of them.

75
00:08:46,873 --> 00:08:48,053
No parents, huh?

76
00:08:49,913 --> 00:08:52,913
I'm sorry to hear that,
kid Well, what's your name?

77
00:08:53,373 --> 00:08:54,773
Nor Okay, nor,

78
00:08:54,873 --> 00:08:58,170
let's see I take it you're heading
to the training academy for classes?

79
00:08:58,253 --> 00:09:02,150
This is the first time I've ever had
a kid your age try to do it before.

80
00:09:02,233 --> 00:09:03,493
What do you mean?

81
00:09:04,233 --> 00:09:05,110
Okay, listen up.

82
00:09:05,193 --> 00:09:07,090
Those registering with the Royal Capitals

83
00:09:07,173 --> 00:09:10,193
Adventures Guild must
take lessons beforehand,

84
00:09:10,773 --> 00:09:13,710
meaning you basically get
training for your job class.

85
00:09:13,793 --> 00:09:15,210
Want to be an adventurer?

86
00:09:15,293 --> 00:09:17,430
You've got to have some skills first.

87
00:09:17,513 --> 00:09:18,490
What kind of skills?

88
00:09:18,573 --> 00:09:21,753
You know, the art of combat
or magic, stuff like that.

89
00:09:23,353 --> 00:09:24,183
Understood!

90
00:09:26,433 --> 00:09:27,473
A swordsman.

91
00:09:29,533 --> 00:09:34,180
Heroes and storybooks can slay a dragon
as big as a mountain in a single swing.

92
00:09:47,813 --> 00:09:48,643
Finally

93
00:10:00,973 --> 00:10:03,032
That's enough, Noor, unfortunately.

94
00:10:03,493 --> 00:10:05,030
Wait, just give me some time!

95
00:10:05,113 --> 00:10:05,943
Forget it.

96
00:10:06,026 --> 00:10:08,307
Going further would be a waste of time.

97
00:10:09,753 --> 00:10:13,812
The only thing you've retained at
all is parrying to evade an attack.

98
00:10:15,313 --> 00:10:18,670
Perhaps it would be wiser if
you were to choose another path.

99
00:10:18,753 --> 00:10:19,583
Who knows?

100
00:10:19,666 --> 00:10:22,280
Your talent may be found
in another capacity.

101
00:10:25,933 --> 00:10:26,763
Warrior.

102
00:10:27,473 --> 00:10:29,630
While fighting with any weapon imaginable,

103
00:10:29,713 --> 00:10:32,390
you risk your life and become
a shield for your allies.

104
00:10:32,473 --> 00:10:34,649
That's pretty close to an adventurer!

105
00:10:43,213 --> 00:10:44,853
I acknowledge your efforts,

106
00:10:45,033 --> 00:10:47,290
but what you have
acquired is only a slight

107
00:10:47,373 --> 00:10:49,770
improvement of your
natural physical abilities.

108
00:10:49,853 --> 00:10:54,147
If you force yourself to continue on,
you could very well lose your life.

109
00:10:55,653 --> 00:10:56,493
A hunter!

110
00:10:57,473 --> 00:11:01,826
I must say, you lack the prudence to
handle any sort of delicate weaponry.

111
00:11:02,933 --> 00:11:03,913
A thief!

112
00:11:04,473 --> 00:11:06,773
You are unable to dismantle the trap,

113
00:11:06,973 --> 00:11:10,753
nor can you sense anyone's presence,
so you cannot become a spy.

114
00:11:12,013 --> 00:11:12,843
Magician!

115
00:11:14,013 --> 00:11:18,013
To think you've come this far, yet
all you can manage is tiny flame.

116
00:11:18,333 --> 00:11:23,098
It's extremely rare to see someone as
incapable of magic as you seem to be, Norn.

117
00:11:24,673 --> 00:11:25,833
A cleric?

118
00:11:34,853 --> 00:11:36,930
Although it only works on minor scratches,

119
00:11:37,013 --> 00:11:39,330
it's still impressive you
became able to use low

120
00:11:39,413 --> 00:11:42,237
-level healing magic
without a natural blessing.

121
00:11:48,733 --> 00:11:51,093
You didn't learn one decent skill?

122
00:11:51,413 --> 00:11:53,850
You spent a full
three-month term practicing

123
00:11:53,933 --> 00:11:57,373
at every training school
and you didn't pass one? No.

124
00:11:59,933 --> 00:12:02,210
Kid, I'm sorry.

125
00:12:02,293 --> 00:12:03,313
I really am.

126
00:12:03,553 --> 00:12:06,259
But I can't let you
register as an adventurer.

127
00:12:08,713 --> 00:12:12,173
I don't have what it takes.

128
00:12:16,873 --> 00:12:18,513
Dad? Mom?

129
00:12:19,513 --> 00:12:20,713
I'm back.

130
00:12:21,813 --> 00:12:26,113
It turns out I have no
talent for anything.

131
00:12:27,793 --> 00:12:28,623
No.

132
00:12:28,793 --> 00:12:32,969
I must take what I've learned and
train harder than I ever have before!

133
00:12:35,733 --> 00:12:40,353
My swordsman instructor told me, if
you practice one skill repeatedly,

134
00:12:40,613 --> 00:12:44,753
over and over, you may be able
to master another skill! Parry!

135
00:12:48,773 --> 00:12:52,597
This is my skill that I acquired
in the swordsman class training.

136
00:12:54,593 --> 00:12:55,793
I will train!

137
00:12:57,233 --> 00:12:59,873
Morning, noon, and night!

138
00:13:09,753 --> 00:13:12,373
I can repel ten swords in one go now.

139
00:13:13,053 --> 00:13:16,753
I don't have any new skills
yet, but I am getting better.

140
00:13:26,693 --> 00:13:28,575
It's a hundred swords in one go.

141
00:13:29,833 --> 00:13:32,421
But I still haven't
acquired any new skills.

142
00:13:34,933 --> 00:13:38,462
At this rate, becoming an
adventurer is nothing but a dream.

143
00:14:00,773 --> 00:14:02,653
I have to try harder.

144
00:14:03,793 --> 00:14:05,853
I must keep training.

145
00:14:19,073 --> 00:14:20,953
These past 14 years,

146
00:14:21,273 --> 00:14:26,013
I have trained every single day, and I
can now parry a thousand wooden swords.

147
00:14:29,473 --> 00:14:32,353
And yet, still no worthy skills.

148
00:14:38,613 --> 00:14:39,813
This is it.

149
00:14:40,133 --> 00:14:41,193
One last try.

150
00:14:47,493 --> 00:14:52,073
Parry, physical enhancement, feather
step, tiny small flame, low heal.

151
00:14:52,693 --> 00:14:55,810
Um, are you sure this is
everything that you have to offer?

152
00:14:55,893 --> 00:14:57,273
Yeah, that's all of it.

153
00:14:57,913 --> 00:15:01,810
Perhaps you may be aware of the Royal
Capital's class training school system.

154
00:15:01,893 --> 00:15:04,370
You can take lessons from any of
our distinguished instructors.

155
00:15:04,453 --> 00:15:05,283
I know.

156
00:15:05,366 --> 00:15:06,830
I've already been through all of them.

157
00:15:06,913 --> 00:15:07,743
Every one?

158
00:15:08,293 --> 00:15:10,890
Um, well, if that's the case, then...

159
00:15:10,973 --> 00:15:13,326
I can't register with your guild, can I?

160
00:15:13,773 --> 00:15:15,590
I'm truly sorry, but I re...

161
00:15:15,673 --> 00:15:17,993
No, you don't need to apologize at all.

162
00:15:22,073 --> 00:15:24,213
I know exactly what I can't do.

163
00:15:25,213 --> 00:15:26,173
Hey, buddy.

164
00:15:26,593 --> 00:15:28,710
Mind not picking on my new employee?

165
00:15:28,793 --> 00:15:31,693
She just started. I'm fine. Oh, hey.

166
00:15:32,033 --> 00:15:33,093
It's been a while.

167
00:15:34,153 --> 00:15:37,213
I have absolutely no idea who you are.

168
00:15:38,473 --> 00:15:40,210
Oh, wait a second.

169
00:15:40,293 --> 00:15:41,393
You're the kid.

170
00:15:41,653 --> 00:15:42,593
You're Noor.

171
00:15:45,433 --> 00:15:49,410
So you mean you've been keeping up with
your own solo training this whole time?

172
00:15:49,493 --> 00:15:54,693
Yeah, but in the end, I've really
only been able to improve my parrying.

173
00:15:55,793 --> 00:15:57,322
Listen to me for a second.

174
00:15:57,453 --> 00:15:59,865
There are different ranks of adventurers.

175
00:16:00,293 --> 00:16:03,533
S-rank being the highest,
and E-rank being the lowest.

176
00:16:03,953 --> 00:16:08,453
To be recognized as an E-rank, you've
got to have one or more useful skills.

177
00:16:09,713 --> 00:16:11,913
But you, you don't have that.

178
00:16:12,833 --> 00:16:15,304
I can't do anything but just give up, huh?

179
00:16:17,873 --> 00:16:20,850
However, that does not mean
you can't be an adventurer.

180
00:16:20,933 --> 00:16:21,763
Are you sure?

181
00:16:21,846 --> 00:16:24,310
There's actually something
lower than E-Rank.

182
00:16:24,393 --> 00:16:25,223
There he is?

183
00:16:25,306 --> 00:16:29,610
The F-Rank, which is basically not talked
about, even for the people doing it.

184
00:16:29,693 --> 00:16:31,470
Okay, then I can register for that one?

185
00:16:31,553 --> 00:16:33,082
There are some conditions.

186
00:16:33,333 --> 00:16:36,230
You're forbidden from taking
any quests that involve

187
00:16:36,313 --> 00:16:39,254
killing anything or venturing
out to gather items.

188
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:42,930
What you can accept are
miscellaneous tasks around the city.

189
00:16:43,013 --> 00:16:45,610
But nobody's dumb enough
to go to the trouble of

190
00:16:45,693 --> 00:16:48,010
becoming an adventurer
just for running errands.

191
00:16:48,093 --> 00:16:51,173
Plus, we also take a cut
for the job placement fee.

192
00:16:51,373 --> 00:16:54,250
You see, it used to be a job
for beggars and vagabonds, so...

193
00:16:54,333 --> 00:16:55,163
I'll do it.

194
00:16:55,873 --> 00:16:58,053
You did hear what I just said, right?

195
00:16:58,373 --> 00:16:59,413
Oh, I don't mind.

196
00:16:59,653 --> 00:17:00,712
Let me take it on.

197
00:17:06,073 --> 00:17:09,213
Then, Noor, here's your
F-Rink adventurer license.

198
00:17:09,813 --> 00:17:10,643
Oh.

199
00:17:13,373 --> 00:17:14,933
Thanks so much!

200
00:17:15,113 --> 00:17:16,760
This means everything to me!

201
00:17:18,653 --> 00:17:19,873
Thanks again!

202
00:17:20,453 --> 00:17:21,773
Strength Enhancement.

203
00:17:27,353 --> 00:17:28,533
Feather Step.

204
00:17:32,613 --> 00:17:34,633
That was scary, huh?

205
00:17:36,013 --> 00:17:36,843
Low Healing.

206
00:17:47,633 --> 00:17:48,613
Tiny flame.

207
00:17:53,973 --> 00:17:54,853
Stone throw.

208
00:18:08,433 --> 00:18:12,853
My dream of becoming an adventurer and
being useful has finally come true.

209
00:18:20,713 --> 00:18:23,693
Anything beyond this
is more than I deserve.

210
00:18:38,093 --> 00:18:41,033
I'll see you again soon, Norf.

211
00:18:49,533 --> 00:18:50,993
Nice work today, Noor.

212
00:18:51,513 --> 00:18:56,213
And thanks to you, we'll have no problem
sticking to the schedule this month.

213
00:18:56,513 --> 00:18:57,807
Yeah, glad to hear it.

214
00:18:59,393 --> 00:19:00,223
Hmm?

215
00:19:00,833 --> 00:19:01,663
What's that?

216
00:19:02,973 --> 00:19:03,803
Someone!

217
00:19:03,886 --> 00:19:04,716
Please help me!

218
00:19:06,573 --> 00:19:07,773
Hey, Noor!

219
00:19:16,353 --> 00:19:18,533
Oh, that's huge.

220
00:19:20,713 --> 00:19:22,889
I've only seen these things in books.

221
00:19:23,053 --> 00:19:25,641
I never thought they
were actually this big.

222
00:19:37,513 --> 00:19:39,410
Surround it and block its movements.

223
00:19:39,493 --> 00:19:40,913
We have to protect her.

224
00:19:50,373 --> 00:19:52,020
Just let him get distracted!

225
00:19:52,593 --> 00:19:53,953
Are you all right?

226
00:19:55,093 --> 00:19:55,923
No.

227
00:19:56,933 --> 00:19:57,973
He's dead.

228
00:20:05,473 --> 00:20:07,355
They're all going to get killed.

229
00:20:27,673 --> 00:20:28,653
Stone throw!

230
00:20:38,273 --> 00:20:39,593
I've got to do it now!

231
00:20:45,453 --> 00:20:46,593
It's fast!

232
00:20:50,313 --> 00:20:51,143
Perry!

233
00:20:59,933 --> 00:21:00,763
Perry!

234
00:21:03,493 --> 00:21:04,873
So much force!

235
00:21:05,233 --> 00:21:07,115
One blow from that and I'm dead!

236
00:21:08,333 --> 00:21:10,370
I need an opening to counterattack!

237
00:21:10,453 --> 00:21:14,213
No, even if there was one,
I have no attack skills.

238
00:21:17,733 --> 00:21:18,593
The girl!

239
00:21:18,973 --> 00:21:20,032
She's still there!

240
00:21:30,173 --> 00:21:31,003
Featherstep!

241
00:21:41,453 --> 00:21:45,413
Even if I cannot become
a true adventurer hero,

242
00:21:46,353 --> 00:21:49,647
I must at least be able to
protect this frightened girl.

243
00:21:50,053 --> 00:21:54,070
No matter the situation, an
adventurer will raise their sword.

244
00:21:54,153 --> 00:21:56,624
and strike down evil for those who cannot.

245
00:21:56,853 --> 00:21:57,933
Remember, son,

246
00:21:58,493 --> 00:22:00,453
that is an adventurer!

247
00:22:03,593 --> 00:22:04,423
Harry!

248
00:22:24,773 --> 00:22:25,853
That was close.

249
00:22:26,293 --> 00:22:29,587
I would definitely have died
if that went on any longer.

250
00:22:31,073 --> 00:22:35,570
And here I thought I could travel the
world and go on adventures at this level.

251
00:22:35,653 --> 00:22:36,633
Yeah, right.

252
00:22:37,073 --> 00:22:39,353
Um, excuse me? Hmm?

253
00:22:39,973 --> 00:22:41,233
Thanks for saving me.

254
00:22:41,493 --> 00:22:43,258
I'm only alive because of you.

255
00:22:44,433 --> 00:22:45,790
I'm glad you survived.

256
00:22:45,873 --> 00:22:47,814
Although it's too bad about them.

257
00:22:49,793 --> 00:22:51,969
Um, sir, may I please have your name?

258
00:22:52,293 --> 00:22:54,133
Oh, I'm not anyone important.

259
00:22:54,713 --> 00:22:55,831
Hey, wait a second!

260
00:22:58,473 --> 00:22:59,793
Thank God you're okay!

261
00:23:00,333 --> 00:23:02,093
Yes, I'm quite safe.

262
00:23:14,893 --> 00:23:16,473
I can't believe it.

263
00:23:16,733 --> 00:23:19,010
I've never seen a cow like that before.

